w: 1.~Here is love, vast as the o- cean, Lov- ing kind- ness as the flood,
w: 2.~On the mount of cru- ci- fix- ion, Foun- tains o- pened deep and wide;
w: 3.~Let me, all Thy love ac- cept- ing, Love Thee, ev- er all my days;
w: 4.~In Thy truth Thou dost di- rect me By Thy Spir- it through Thy Word;
[V:1] [DF] [EG] | "F"[FA]3 [CF] [DG] [FA] | "Bb"[DG] [DF]3 [DF] [B,D] | "F"[A,C]3 [CF] "C"[EG] [CE] | "F"[CF]4 
w: When the Prince of Life, our Ran- som, Shed for us His pre- cious blood.
w: Through the flood- gates of God's mer- cy Flowed a vast and gra- cious tide.
w: Let me seek Thy king- dom on- ly, And my life be to Thy praise;
w: And Thy grace my need is meet- ing As I trust in Thee, my Lord.
[V:1] [FA] [FB] | "F"[Fc]3 [FA] [GB] [FA] | "C"[FA] [EG]3 [EG] [FA] | "Gm"[FB]3 [DG] "C7"[EA] [EB] | "F"[FA]4 
w: Who His love will not re- mem- ber? Who can cease to sing His praise?
w: Grace and love, like might- y riv- ers, Poured in- ces- sant from a- bove,
w: Thou a- lone shalt be my glo- ry, Noth- ing in the world I see;
w: Of Thy full- ness Thou art pour- ing Thy great love and pow'r on me,
[V:1] [FA] [EG] | "Dm"[DF]3 [DG] [DF] [CE] | "Bb"[B,D] [DF]3 [DF] [DG] | "F"[FA]3 [DF] "C"[EG] [CE] | "F"[CF]4 |]
w: He can nev- er be for- got- ten, Through- out heav'n's e- ter- nal days.
w: And heav'n's peace and per- fect jus- tice Kissed a guilt- y world in love.
w: Thou hast cleansed and sanc- ti- fied me, Thou Thy- self hast set me free.
w: With- out meas- ure, full and bound- less, Draw- ing out my heart to Thee.
